<attribute name="version" nodeId="277da289"></attribute>
<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="6c96acf">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Review current Requirements Traceability Matrix (RTM)&amp;nbsp;for referential integrity
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Verify that all known requirements have been documented, i.e. scope updates have been incorporated into the RTM
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Review current test case inventory
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Reconcile RTM with test case inventory
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Resolve any discrepancies found by updating the RTM or creating new test cases as required
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Submit updated RTM for approval
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        RTM can be maintained using test management tools (ex: HP ALM)
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="35348c2a"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="f39ab4d2">&lt;p&gt;
    The RTM is tracking requirements from identification to process decomposition, to solution object, to test case.
    Mapping requirements to test is the logical conclusion.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Mapping all requirements gathered throughout the planning and design sessions to specific test cases is a key activity
    to validate the designed target solution translates into the&amp;nbsp;implemented solution and is fit for purpose.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Traceability may be captured manually with spreadsheets or with testing software. If the project is using testing
    software there may be a data field to list the requirement; if this is not available, the mapping of requirements to
    test should be tracked manually.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Each functional team is responsible to make sure each and every requirement is linked to one or more test cases. In the
    end, traceability should be established to demonstrate to stakeholders that all requirements have been tested.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="73a0c3a1"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="b178443b">To validate that&amp;nbsp;functional and technical requirements have been identified and are accounted for in one or more test
scripts.</attribute>
<attribute name="alternatives" nodeId="9a3a6a02"></attribute>
</Element>
